# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Client-safe Supabase credentials (used in the browser).
# These are PUBLIC by design — Row Level Security (RLS) is what
# actually protects your data, not secrecy of these values.
# Find both in: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-PUBLIC-KEY

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This project does NOT use the Supabase service-role key anywhere.
# Do not add SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to this app.
# If you ever add a feature that needs it, it must only be read
# inside a server-only file (e.g. a Route Handler) and must never
# be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
